# Git commit rules (mandatory for agents)

Applies to **Cursor**, **Claude Code**, **Codex**, and any other agent opening a PR for teammates.

## Never ship a squash blob

- **Do not** land feature work as one fat commit (or a handful of "WIP" / "address feedback" squash commits).
- **Do** split every PR into many small, reviewable commits before you push / open / update the PR.
- If you already made a mega-commit: soft-reset to the base branch, then recommit in layers (preserve the working tree — never `reset --hard` with uncommitted feature work).

## Granularity (this is the bar)

For a medium/large PR, **default to one commit per file** (or one tiny cohesive pair: e.g. `db/foo.ts` + its `index.ts` export).

| Smell | Action |
|-------|--------|
| 1 commit covers many unrelated paths | Resplit |
| One commit is hundreds of lines across folders | Resplit |
| ~3–4k line PR with only ~10–20 commits | **Too coarse** — go file-level |
| Commit mixes migration + UI + agent + tests | Resplit |

Rough check before push:

```
changed_lines / commit_count
```

If that average is **well over ~150–200 lines/commit** on a multi-file PR, keep splitting. A 3.8k-line PR should usually be **dozens** of commits, not a dozen.

## Required commit message prefixes

First token of the subject line must be one of:

| Prefix | Use for |
|--------|---------|
| `(feature)` | New user-facing or API capability |
| `(bug)` | Fix incorrect behavior |
| `(cleanup)` | Dead code, formatting-only, remove cruft |
| `(docs)` | Rules, skills, README, comments-only docs |
| `(refactor)` | Restructure with no intended behavior change |
| `(test)` | Tests only (no production code) |
| `(chore)` | Tooling, deps, CI, env samples |
| `(internal)` | Operator/internal tooling that is not product UX |

Examples:

```
(feature) add account_links / account_sessions migration
(feature) add createAccountLink db helper
(feature) add hashed token helpers for account challenges
(bug) use production site URL for pay links
(test) cover verifyAccountLink single-use redeem
(docs) require agents to split PR commits file-by-file
```

## How to split (dependency order)

1. Docs / agent rules (if part of the same PR)
2. Each migration file → its own commit
3. Each schema / `db/` file → its own commit (index re-exports can ride with the new helper, or alone)
4. Each `libs/` file → its own commit
5. Each API route / page / component file → its own commit
6. Each agent wiring file → its own commit
7. Each test file → its own `(test)` commit

Do **not** batch an entire domain folder into one commit just because files share a directory.

## Workflow checklist (every PR)

Before opening or updating a PR for teammates:

1. `git log origin/<base>..HEAD --oneline` + `git diff --stat origin/<base>` — if commits ≪ files, **resplit**.
2. Stage with pathspecs (`git add path1`), almost never `git add -A` for mixed work.
3. Commit with a prefixed subject a reviewer can skim in `git log`.
4. Prefer **merge commit** (or rebase+ff) into main — do not squash-merge away the split history when teammates asked for it.

## What “done” looks like

A teammate can walk `git log --oneline` file-by-file and review without opening a 3k-line blob. Each commit is one reviewable idea, usually one file.
